    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0001",
      "sequence": 984,
      "meaning": "One day alone remains of the appointed exile. Bharata's mind is overwhelmed by sorrow as he wonders why his Lord has not returned—whether Rama has judged him crooked and forgotten him. He calls Lakshmana blessed for his devotion to Rama's lotus feet and fears that his own conduct has made the Lord leave him behind. Yet he trusts Rama's tender nature: the friend of the lowly never holds a servant's faults against him. Auspicious signs assure him they will meet; if he remains alive after the deadline, no one in the world will be more fallen.",
