    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0002",
      "sequence": 985,
      "meaning": "Seeing Bharata, Hanuman rejoices; his body thrills and tears fill his eyes. In nectar-like speech he announces that Rama—whose separation Bharata mourns day and night—has defeated the enemy and is returning safely with Sita and Lakshmana while the gods sing his fame. Bharata's sorrow vanishes like a thirsty person's on receiving nectar. Hanuman identifies himself as the Wind-god's son and Rama's servant. Bharata rises, embraces him with reverence and love, and says that no gift could repay such news. At Bharata's request Hanuman recounts Rama's deeds; Bharata then asks whether the compassionate Lord ever remembers him as a servant.",
