    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0003",
      "sequence": 986,
      "meaning": "Delighted, Bharata returns to Ayodhya, gives the news to the guru, the palace and all the mothers, and assures them that Rama is well and approaching. Men and women hurry out joyfully with auspicious offerings—curd, sacred grass, pigment, fruit, flowers and fresh tulasi leaves—in golden trays, singing as they go with stately gait. Children and elders run as they are, asking one another whether they have seen merciful Raghuraya. Knowing that the Lord is coming, Ayodhya becomes a treasury of beauty; pleasant threefold breezes blow and the Sarayu's waters grow exceptionally clear.",
