    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0004",
      "sequence": 987,
      "meaning": "Rama, the sun that opens the lotus of the solar dynasty, shows the lovely city to the monkeys. He tells Sugriva, Angada and Vibhishana that although everyone praises Vaikuntha and the Vedas and Puranas make it known, no place is as dear to him as Ayodhya—a truth few understand. It is his beautiful birthplace, with the purifying Sarayu flowing to its north; those who bathe there effortlessly attain residence near him. Its people are especially dear to him, and the city itself bestows his abode and is a mass of joy. The monkeys rejoice to hear Rama praise blessed Ayodhya.",
