    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0005",
      "sequence": 988,
      "meaning": "Bharata and the people arrive, their bodies lean from separation from Raghubira. Rama sees the sages Vamadeva and Vasishtha, lays bow and arrows upon the ground, rushes forward and, with Lakshmana, clasps the guru's lotus feet, his body thrilled. Asked about his welfare, Rama says that it rests entirely in the sage's grace. The upholder of dharma bows to all the Brahmins. Bharata then grasps the lotus feet revered by gods, sages, Shiva and Brahma and lies upon the ground, refusing to rise until the ocean of compassion lifts and embraces him. Hair stands on Rama's dark body and tears flood his fresh-lotus eyes.",
