    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0006",
      "sequence": 989,
      "meaning": "Bharata and his younger brother meet Lakshmana and erase the unbearable grief born of separation. Bharata bows his head at Sita's feet and, with his brother, receives supreme joy. Seeing Rama, Ayodhya's people rejoice and every calamity of separation disappears. Noticing that all are overcome with love, the compassionate slayer of Khara performs a wonder: he manifests countless forms and meets each person appropriately. Raghubira's merciful glance leaves every man and woman free of sorrow. In a moment the Lord meets them all—Uma, no one knows this mystery—then, having made everyone happy, Rama moves on, the abode of character and virtue. Kausalya and the other mothers run toward him like cows released at sight of their calves.",
