    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0007",
      "sequence": 990,
      "meaning": "Vaidehi meets all her mothers-in-law and joyfully bows at their feet. They ask after her welfare and bless her: may her married good fortune remain unbroken. Everyone gazes at Raghupati's lotus face and, treating the moment as auspicious, restrains tears of joy. They perform arati in golden trays, look repeatedly at the Lord's body and make offerings in many ways, their hearts filled with supreme bliss. Kausalya gazes again and again at compassionate, battle-firm Raghubira and wonders how her two tender boys could have killed Lanka's immensely powerful demon warriors.",
