    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0008",
      "sequence": 991,
      "meaning": "Vibhishana, Sugriva, Nala, Nila, Jambavan, Angada, Hanuman and the other monkey heroes assume attractive human forms. With deep respect they praise Bharata's love, character, vows and discipline; seeing the citizens' ways, they all commend their love for the Lord's feet. Rama summons his companions and instructs them to bow to the sage. He identifies Vasishtha as the revered guru of his line, by whose grace the demons were defeated, and tells the sage that these friends served as boats across the ocean of battle, risked their lives for him and are dearer to him even than Bharata. Hearing him, all are absorbed as fresh joy arises every moment.",
