      "sequence": 992,
      "meaning": "The citizens decorate golden vessels and place them at their doors. They fashion festoons, flags and banners for the auspicious occasion, sprinkle every street with fragrance and fill ceremonial designs with auspicious gems. The city resounds with many instruments. Women everywhere offer gifts and blessings with joy-filled hearts; adorned young women carry varied golden arati trays and sing auspicious songs. They worship the remover of distress, the sun to the lotus-forest of Raghu's line. Even the Vedas, Shesha and Sarasvati—celebrated describers of a city's beauty, prosperity and blessing—would stand transfixed by this sight; how then can ordinary people describe his glory?",
