      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0010",
      "sequence": 993,
      "meaning": "Knowing that Kaikeyi feels ashamed, Rama first goes to her house, consoles her at length and gives her great happiness; only then does Hari enter his own palace. When the ocean of compassion reaches the palace, every man and woman in the city is happy. Guru Vasishtha summons the Brahmins and declares that this is an auspicious day and hour: they should joyfully authorize Ramachandra to sit upon the throne. The sages delight in his pleasing words and say that Rama's consecration brings joy to the world; there should now be no delay in applying the royal mark to the king.",
